  "notes": "Source: official 2024-2025 Bastyr University catalog, Master of Acupuncture (quarter system; 11 quarters sequenced exactly as the catalog's quarterly tables print them). The catalog's published graduation total is 165.5 credits = 124 core + 4 elective + 37.5 clinic; this seed sequences 161.5 credits and the 4 elective credits are not assigned to any quarter in the catalog, so total_credits is the sum of sequenced course credits only. Course category rule (matches the catalog's published 37.5 clinic credits): clinic = the three observation rotations (AM5801/AM5802/AM6800), the preceptorship shift (AM6801), all AOM Clinic shifts, and Interim Clinic; AOM Clinic Entry is didactic core. Catalog scheduling notes: AM6800 may be taken winter of year one or fall of year two; AM6801 may be taken any time after completion of AM5801 or AM6800 (sequenced as printed). Graduation: 3.0 GPA, completion within five years, at least two-thirds of credits in residence.",
